cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Golden-ratio growth of Conway's subprime closure"
message: If you use this paper or the Lean formalization, please cite them as below.
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Popescu
    given-names: Romain
    email: rep2159@columbia.edu
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science, Columbia University"
date-released: 2026-09-12
license: Apache-2.0
url: https://github.com/Renriviera/conway-subprime-golden
abstract: >-
  Let s(m) be the Conway subprime function, define x ∘ y = s(x+y), and let
  C_0 = {1}, C_{n+1} = C_n ∪ (C_n ∘ C_n). We prove the Caragiu–Vicol–Zaki
  conjecture that |C_{n+1}| / |C_n| tends to the golden ratio.
keywords:
  - Conway subprime function
  - golden ratio
  - Goldbach-type theorems
  - Hardy–Littlewood circle method
  - Lean
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "Golden-ratio growth of Conway's subprime closure"
